  "id": "COMPOUND:30382 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions linking the compound to the Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform. The compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including Quinaldic Acid and N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide, both of which are known to interact with the target protein. Additionally, the compound is linked to G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1, which is also a target of several compounds that ultimately interact with the same phosphatase. This suggests a potential pathway where the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the phosphatase, possibly through indirect mechanisms involving receptor activation or downstream signaling. The evidence supports a role for the compound in influencing the activity of the phosphatase, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
